        "original_id": "75051190-ddf8-581a-a154-dffafd6aee5f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Antonio Salieri\n- Works: Giulio Sabino, Prima la musica e poi le parole\n- Places: Legnago, Verona, Republic of Venice, Habsburg Monarchy\n- Topics: opera parody, 18th-century European staging\n\nFacts:\n- At the end of the 18th century, the opera Giulio Sabino was staged in six or seven European countries.\n- In 1786, Antonio Salieri's work Prima la musica e poi le parole parodied Giulio Sabino.\n- Antonio Salieri was an Italian classical composer, conductor, and teacher.\n- Antonio Salieri was born on 18 August 1750 in Legnago, south of Verona, in the Republic of Venice.\n- Antonio Salieri spent his adult life and career as a subject of the Habsburg Monarchy.\n- Antonio Salieri died on 7 May 1825.",
